      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Retraining programs are a band-aid on a systemic wound; they assume that displaced workers can always pivot to jobs that AI hasn't already optimized away. While taxing AI companies is a necessary component, it is insufficient on its own because it doesn't guarantee income for the millions who lose their jobs instantly. UBI is the only solution because it addresses the core problem—the decoupling of productivity from human labor—by ensuring everyone benefits from the wealth generated by automation.",
